  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: The latest round of daytime \nthunderstorms continues over far eastern and northeastern Nevada\ntoday. Given the previous few days, any thunderstorms have a high\nprobability of new fire ignitions from lightning strikes. This \npattern will continue through Thursday as the high pressure system\nshifts west. Starting Friday, a trough in the northwest will \ncombine with the high over Arizona and New Mexico to bring \nsouthwest flow and Pacific moisture into the forecast area. The \nstrength of this moisture is still being determined but the \ncurrent forecast would bring shower and thunderstorm chances to \neffectively the entire forecast area between Friday and Saturday. \nMoisture is currently anticipated to linger into early next week, \nwith weaker and more sparse storms Sunday and Monday.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Moderate confidence in storm\nchances and associated impacts through Thursday. High confidence\nin increasing moisture and atmospheric instability for Friday and\nSaturday but low confidence in moisture strength and extent of\nimpacts. No changes to NBM output.",
